# Pass-1 U01 part C: outcomes for items processed in the continuation (executed first in record script).
R("Z1655", "nothing", "Strengthening 'every 4/p has an ES triple with a prime y or z' is FALSE at small p: over primes ≤5000 (667), 302 have no such triple; smallest failures 7, 13, 31, 37, 43, 61.", ["scripts/z52b_p1_U01_stats2.py", "data/z52b/pass1/U01/allsols_5000.txt.gz"], "")
R("Z1941", "interesting", "Minimal max denominator over ES triples, scaled by p: dyadic maxima of min-max/p are 68 (p∈[100,300)), 290 (p=577), 561 (p=2243), 1014 (p=4049); log–log slope of min-max/p vs p is 0.54 over 667 primes ≤5000. So the smallest max(x,y,z) grows like p^{1.5}, not p(log p)^A, at this range. Caveat: exhaustive enumeration limited to p≤5000.", ["scripts/z52b_p1_U01_allsols.py", "scripts/z52b_p1_U01_stats2.py", "data/z52b/pass1/U01/allsols_5000.txt.gz"], "Extend enumeration to p≤2e4 (cost ~1 min per 5000) and test slope 0.5 vs 0.54 to see whether it stabilises at 1/2 (i.e. min-max ~ p^{3/2}).")
R("Z3154", "nothing", "min over ES triples of max-denominator, normalised by p²: dyadic maxima 0.274 ([100,300)), 0.503 (p=577), 0.250 ([1000,3000)), 0.250 ([3000,9000)); median over primes ≤5000 is 0.037. The p²-normalised max does not decay; the 0.5 value at 577 is a single sporadic prime.", ["scripts/z52b_p1_U01_stats2.py", "data/z52b/pass1/U01/allsols_5000.txt.gz"])
R("Z2232", "nothing", "Increasing-denominator convention (x≤y≤z) gives median count U=62 over primes ≤5000; 50.7% of primes have a solution with two equal denominators (isosceles law, Z0973). Ordered-count recomputation not needed for the convention question.", ["scripts/z52b_p1_U01_stats2.py", "data/z52b/pass1/U01/allsols_5000.txt.gz"])
R("Z2372", "nothing", "Three-fold sums 1/x+1/y+1/z with x,y,z ≤300 (mod 2^61−1 hash): 4146463 distinct values; 4/n is in the set for 237 of 299 n ≤300. The misses include primes 37, 47, 53, 59, 61, 67, 71, 73, 79, 83, i.e. the bounded-denominator sumset does not contain 4/p for many p with small denominators.", ["scripts/z52b_p1_U01_stats2.py"], "Energy E(R) of the reciprocal set R={1/x:x≤N} vs |sumset| at N=300 is the natural next measurement.")
R("Z3114", "nothing", "Numerator sets A_p∩[5,48] for 9589 primes: 763 distinct sets; most A_p are nearly full (size 44 is the mode with 7001 primes), so unions of two sets land in the family 72682/79800 times trivially. Union-closure is uninformative for this family; the complement family (failure sets F(m)) is the non-trivial object.", ["scripts/z52b_p1_U01_stats2.py"])
R("Z1944", "interesting", "Four-term rescue (x≤y≤z plus a fourth term w ≤ p³, minimal max(x,y,z)) for primes 5≤p≤150 (distinct x<y<z) is ~0.05–0.5 of the 3-term min-max R(p): median ratio 0.047, e.g. p=53: 40 vs R=742; p=59: 45 vs 885. The rescued largest term is ≈0.75p, so allowing one huge fourth denominator removes the p^{1.5} scale.", ["scripts/z52b_p1_U01_rescue.py", "data/z52b/pass1/U01/allsols_5000.txt.gz"], "Test whether min max(x,y,z)/p tends to a constant on p≤2000 and identify the extremal (x,y,z).")
R("Z0138", "nothing", "Distinct-denominator 4-term reps of 4/n, n ≤80: least C_n = min over reps of max-denominator / n is ≤9 for all n ≤80 (largest C_59=9, C_73=C_67=C_53=7). Not tested for growth beyond n=80; with the non-distinct convention the answer is trivially 1 (x=y=z=w=n).", ["scripts/z52b_p1_U01_four.py"], "Run n≤400 to see whether max C_n grows (e.g. like log n).")
R("Z0309", "nothing", "16/n as a sum of 4 distinct unit fractions (equivalently 4/n with all four denominators divisible by 4) fails only for n ∈ {2,3,4,5,6,7,17} among n ≤80.", ["scripts/z52b_p1_U01_four.py"])
R("Z0136", "nothing", "PROVED: no ES triple has pairwise coprime denominators for an odd prime p. From 4xyz = p(xy+yz+zx): if y,z,x are pairwise coprime, mod y gives y | p·zx hence y∈{1,p}, and likewise for x,z, leaving only degenerate triples. Numerically: 0 of 76 primes ≤400 have such a triple (scripts/z52b_p1_U01_triples.py).", ["scripts/z52b_p1_U01_triples.py"])
R("Z0902", "nothing", "PROVED: no ES triple has a denominator x with x | yz±1 unless x∈{1,p}: mod x, 4xyz ≡ 0 gives x | p·yz, and yz ≡ ∓1 then forces x | p. Numerically 0 triples among primes ≤400 (76 primes).", ["scripts/z52b_p1_U01_triples.py"])
R("Z0311", "nothing", "4/p − 1/x as a sum of two distinct prime-reciprocals 1/q1+1/q2 for some x∈[p/4,p]: 0 of 76 primes ≤400. The prime-denominator two-term completion never occurs at this scale.", ["scripts/z52b_p1_U01_triples.py"])
R("Z0680", "nothing", "Second implementation (two-term divisor method) reproduces raw U_m(p) for m=7..13 at all primes ≤400 (0 mismatches). OEIS submission itself not a pass-1 step.", ["scripts/z52b_p1_U01_triples.py", "data/z52b/raw/m7_pr1e5.txt", "data/z52b/raw/m13_pr1e5.txt"])
R("Z0104", "nothing", "Egyptian length over ℤ (distinct unit fractions, length ≤3 tested) for coprime a<b, a≤8, b≤40: length 1: 39, length 2: 97, length 3: 47, >3: 2. The F_3[T] comparison is not run in this pass.", ["scripts/z52b_p1_U01_triples.py"], "")
